                "caption": "Figure 1:GlanceNav at a glance.(a)Step-wise navigators repeatedly encode sampled historical frames at each decision.(b)GlanceNav encodes each frame once, maintaining a recurrent state alongside a fixed-size window of recent observations and selected keyframes. This design enables episode-level training with the same memory mechanism used at inference. Step latency is measured on an RTX PRO 6000, using StageVLN[7]with a similarly sized backbone as the baseline.(c)Success rates (SR) of single-RGB navigators on R2R-CE val-unseen (seeTab.1). Arrows indicate improvements across our three training stages.++1B denotes an additional geometry encoder.",
